QmClient
--------

QmClient is graphic tool to browse the configuration of Pirelli/ADB Routers.
QmClient is written with the Qt framework (version 4 or 5) to be
platform independent, both Linux and Windows are supported (OS X coming soon).

To fetch data from the router the tool needs to communicate with cm via TCP.
By default cm binds the port 9034 on the loopback interface,
so a TCP proxy is needed to connect to the daemon.

The simplest way is to copy in the board a tool named datapipe
which listens on an interface and connects to another one like this:
datapipe 192.168.1.1 9034 127.0.0.1 9034
This requires the datapipe to be started at every reboot.

A better and permanent solution is to compile a build with
CONFIG_PACKAGE_yaps-gui-sdk=m
This will let cm bind all the interfaces, and QmClient can connect directly.
